{"id":"word:hebrew:H669","type":"word","title":"אֶפְרַיִם","subtitle":"H669 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Ephrajim , a son of Joseph; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֶפְרַיִם (H669) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 180 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֶפְרַיִם (ʼEphrayim) means Ephrajim , a son of Joseph; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory First listed occurrence: 1Chr 6 51."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֶפְרַיִם","transliteration":"ʼEphrayim","pronunciation":"ef-rah'-yim","strong":"H669","lemmaId":"hebrew:H669","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["אֶפְרַ֔יִם","אֶפְרָ֑יִם","אֶפְרַ֖יִם","אֶפְרַ֨יִם֙","אֶפְרָֽיִם"],"morphs":[["HNp",149],["HR/Np",17],["HC/Np",13],["HC/R/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Ephrajim , a son of Joseph; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory","usage":"Ephraim, Ephraimites.","full":"H669. Ephrayim אֶפְרַ֫יִם proper name, masculine Ephraim ( Gen 41:52 connected with הִפְרָה , Hiph`il of פרה , compare פרא Hiph`il Hosea 13:15 ). 1 2nd son of Joseph Gen 41:52 ; 46:20 ; reckoned among sons of Jacob, blessed by him, and given preference over Manasseh 48:1 , 5 , 13 , 14 , 17 (twice in verse) (compare 48:19 ) 48:20 ; 48:20 ; 50:23 ; Num 1:10 ; 1Chr 7:20 , 22 . 2 אֶפְרַיִם בְּנֵי (= descendants, tribe of east) Num 1:32 ; 2:18 (twice in verse); 2:24 ; 7:48 ; 10:22 ; 26:35 , 37 ; Josh 16:5 , 9 (boundaries of territory), 17:8 ; 1Chr 9:3 ; 12:31 ; 27:10 , 14 , 20 ; 2Chr 28:12 ; less often א ׳מַטֵּה Num 1:33 ; 13:8 ; Josh 21:5 ; 1Chr 6:51 ; בְנֵיאֿ ׳מַטֵּה Num 34:24 ; Josh 16:8 ; compare 14:4 ; א ׳שֵׁבֶט Psa 78:67 (|| יוֺסֵף אֹהֶל ); א ׳בֵּית Judg 10:9 ; also ׳א alone, tribe Ephraim Num 26:28 ; Deut 33:17 ; Josh 16:10 + often; א ׳אֶרֶין וּמְנַשֶּׁה 17:17 compare Judg 12:15 ; 2Chr 30:10 especially 3 הַראֶֿפְרַיִם the mountain-country of Ephraim , a ridge stretching from north to south through territory assigned to Ephraim, with fruitful land on both slopes, especially the western (compare Di Josh 16:1 ) 17:15 ; 19:50 ; 20:7 ; Judg 2:9 ; 3:27 ; 4:5 26t. 4 by Hosea & Isaiah (rarely later) אֶפְרַיִם = kingdom of northern Israel (from Ephraim as largest & strongest tribe in it) Hosea 4:17 ; 5:3 (twice in verse); 5:5 (|| יִשְׂרָאֵל ) 5:11 ; 5:12 30t. Hosea; Isa 7:2 , 5 , 8 , 9 , 17 9 t. Isaiah; also Jer 7:15 ; 31:9 , 18 , 20 ; Ezek 37:16 (strike out Co) 37:19 ; Psa 78:9 ; 2Chr 25:7 , 10 ; compare 30:1 ; Psa 60:9 = 108:9 ; א ׳עָרֵי 2Chr 17:2 ; compare 34:6 ; א ׳שְׂדֵה Obadiah 19; hence ׳א alone in local sense 31:1 ; also Hosea 5:9 , where feminine (& perhaps Isa 7:2 ). 5 אֶפְרַיִם יִעַר 2Sam 18:6 , east of Jordan; ᵐ5 L Klo read מַחֲנַיִם יער compare 17:24 , 27 . 6 name of a city near Baal-hazor 2Sam 13:23 (= Ἐφραϊμ John 11:54 & 1 Macc 11:34? Klo compare ᵐ5 L Γοφραιμ & עפרון , Qr עֶפְרַיִן 2Chr 13:9 ; so previously Bö Th Ke compare Dr). 7 אֶפְרַיִם שַׁעַר a chief gate of Jerusalem 2Kin 14:13 ; 2Chr 25:23 ; Neh 8:16 ; 12:39 ; perhaps at northwest angle, near Holy Sepulchre, compare Schick-Guthe ZPV 1885 . אֶפְרָת see אפרתה . below","rootNote":"dual of masculine form of 672 ; double fruit ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 6 51","keyReferences":["1Chr 6 51","1Chr 6 52","1Chr 7 20","1Chr 7 22","1Chr 9 3","1Chr 12 31","1Chr 27 10","1Chr 27 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":180,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 6 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶפְרָֽיִם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 52","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":52,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶפְרָ֑יִם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 7 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":7,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":